#: ../../infrastructure/loadbalancers/lb.rst:138
msgid ""
"Morpheus exposes configuration options during provisioning of an Instance "
"relevant and common to each supported LB Integration. In some cases, "
"Morpheus also provides direct management and sync support for VIP "
"configurations on the various Load Balancers (such as F5, and NSX Advanced "
"Load Balancer), However in a day to day orchestrated workflow this would not"
" be the ideal means by which a user should consume load balancer services."
msgstr ""
"Morpheus exposes configuración opciones durante provisioning de un Instancia"
" relevant y común a cada soportado LB Integración. En algunos cases, "
"Morpheus también proporciona direct gestión y sync support para VIP "
"configurations en el varios Balanceadores de carga (como F5, y NSX Advanced "
"Balanceador de carga), However en un day a day orchestrated workflow este "
"would no be el ideal means por cual un usuario debería consume load balancer"
" servicios."

#: ../../infrastructure/loadbalancers/lb.rst:140
msgid ""
"By tying the Load Balancer associations into the provisioning of instances "
"and the definition of the instance catalog item, the lifecycle of the VIP "
"can more easily be maintained throughout the lifecycle of whatever "
"application may be deployed."
msgstr ""
"Por tying el Balanceador de carga associations en el provisioning de "
"instances y el definition del instance catalog elemento, el lifecycle del "
"VIP puede más easily be maintained throughout el lifecycle de whatever "
"aplicación puede be desplegado."

#: ../../infrastructure/loadbalancers/lb.rst:143
msgid "Setting up an Instance for Load Balancer Consumption"
msgstr "Setting up un Instancia para Balanceador de carga Consumption"

#: ../../infrastructure/loadbalancers/lb.rst:145
msgid ""
"Several of the provided Morpheus instance types are ready to go with load "
"balancer orchestration out of the box (Apache, Nginx, Tomcat, Node.js, etc)."
" It is also fairly easy to extend existing generic instance types during "
"provisioning to be tied to load balancers or to set up said catalog items in"
" advanced for such functionality."
msgstr ""
"Varios del proporcionado Morpheus instance tipos son listo a go con load "
"balancer orchestration de forma predeterminada (Apache, Nginx, Tomcat, "
"Node.js, etc). It es también fairly easy a extend existente generic instance"
" tipos durante provisioning a be tied a load balancers o a establecer up "
"said catalog elementos en advanced para such functionality."

#: ../../infrastructure/loadbalancers/lb.rst:147
msgid ""
"When creating a custom Instance Type (in |Lib|), one can define a list of "
"exposed ports that the node type within the instance exposes.  When defining"
" these exposed ports it prompts for a Name, Port Number, and LB Type. The LB"
" Type is what enables load-balancer functionality. This can either be "
"HTTP,HTTPS, or TCP. This specification helps build the correct profile for "
"the VIP as well as setup the appropriate types of Health Monitors within the"
" target load balancer integration."
msgstr ""
"Cuando creating un personalizado Instancia Tipo (en |Lib|), one puede define"
" un lista de exposed puertos ese el nodo tipo dentro de el instance exposes."
"  Cuando defining estos exposed puertos it prompts para un Nombre, Port "
"Número, y LB Tipo. El LB Tipo es qué habilita load-balancer functionality. "
"Este puede cualquiera be HTTP,HTTPS, o TCP. Este specification helps build "
"el correct profile para el VIP así como setup el appropriate tipos de Health"
" Monitors dentro de el destino load balancer integration."

#: ../../infrastructure/loadbalancers/lb.rst:149
msgid ""
"Now, when a user consumes this custom instance type (either through single "
"instance provisioning or full application blueprint provisioning), a section"
" appears in the Automation phase of provisioning. Each port that is defined "
"that exposes a load-balancer gets a dropdown to choose which load balancer "
"integration attach to the exposed port and various prompts become available."
msgstr ""
"Ahora, cuando un usuario consumes este personalizado instance tipo "
"(cualquiera a través de single instance provisioning o completo aplicación "
"blueprint provisioning), un sección aparece en el Automation phase de "
"provisioning. Cada puerto ese es definido ese exposes un load-balancer "
"obtiene un dropdown a elegir cual load balancer integration attach al "
"exposed puerto y varios prompts become disponible."

#: ../../infrastructure/loadbalancers/lb.rst:151
msgid ""
"These prompts control features ranging from target VIP Address to selecting "
"an SSL Certificate to be applied to the VIP. These SSL Certificates will "
"even go so far as to create SSL Profiles in integrations for things like an "
"F5 automatically for the application."
msgstr ""
"Estos prompts control funciones ranging desde destino VIP Address a "
"selecting un Certificado SSL a be applied al VIP. Estos Certificados SSL "
"será incluso go así far como a crear SSL Profiles en integrations para "
"things like un F5 automáticamente para el aplicación."

#: ../../infrastructure/loadbalancers/lb.rst:153
msgid ""
"Once the instance is provisioned, as part of the final phase, the load "
"balancer configuration will be applied and maintained on the instance. This "
"association can be manipulated after the fact via the \"Scale\" tab found on"
" the Instance Detail page."
msgstr ""
"Once el instance es aprovisionado, como part del final phase, el load "
"balancer configuración será be applied y maintained en el instance. Este "
"association puede be manipulated después de el fact via el \"Scale\" pestaña"
" found en el Instancia Detail página."

#: ../../infrastructure/loadbalancers/lb.rst:155
msgid ""
"Another benefit to associating load-balancers this way is that the pool "
"members are automatically maintained during scaling events, either via auto-"
"scaling thresholds or manual node additions / removals."
msgstr ""
"Another benefit a associating load-balancers este way es ese el pool "
"miembros son automáticamente maintained durante scaling eventos, cualquiera "
"via auto-scaling thresholds o manual nodo additions / removals."

